  executionSurface: modalities::logic::deontic;
  curationStatus: Proposed;
  @condition: (c) if the person has applied for an IC review in relation to the decision: (i) proceedings in relation to the IC review are concluded; and (ii) the time for applying to the Tribunal for a review in relation to the decision has ended, if the person has not applied for such a review; or (iii) the time for instituting an appeal to the Federal Court in relation to the IC review has ended (with no appeal instituted), or, if an appeal has been instituted, all proceedings in relation to the appeal have been concluded;;
  @action: The IC review and Federal Court appeal proceedings must be concluded.;
}

freedom-of-information-amendment-reform-act-2010-sch-3-sec-18-logic-73 {
